      "position": 0,
      "content": "TRANSFER INFORMATION",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "df7b6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "Thank you for your interest in Sacramento State! This articulation agreement displays the lower-division courses required in the major: Sacramento State courses on the left and approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right. Although completion of the coursework listed below is not mandatory prior to admission, students are advised to complete as much lower-division course preparation as possible prior to transfer. Additional Resources: See the University Catalog for the full listing of degree requirements for this major. Visit our Sac State Apply page for more information about our campus! Visit the Admissions website for current transfer admission requirements. Connect with an Admissions Counselor .",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(29, 32, 36); font-size: 14px;\">Thank you for your interest in Sacramento State! </strong></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This articulation agreement displays the lower-division courses required in the major: Sacramento State courses on the left and approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right. Although completion of the coursework listed below is not mandatory prior to admission, students are advised to complete as much lower-division course preparation as possible prior to transfer. </span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Additional Resources:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://catalog.csus.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>University Catalog</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> for the full listing of degree requirements for this major.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Visit our </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Sac State Apply</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> page for more information about our campus!</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Visit the </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/admissions/application-process/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Admissions website</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> for current transfer admission requirements. </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Connect with an </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/admissions/connect-with-admissions.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Admissions Counselor</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">. </span></li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "id": "627a6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "MAJOR INFORMATION",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "637a6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "The B.A. in Spanish requires a \"C\" or higher in all courses applied to the major. Students interested in majoring in Spanish should demonstrate proficiency in the language through the second semester of intermediate level study prior to beginning upper-division courses. The Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Spanish is compatible with the B.A. in Spanish at Sacramento State. Students pursuing the Associate Degree for Transfer must complete all lower-division major coursework with a \"C\" or better. Study Abroad: Students with an overall 2.75 GPA or higher are eligible to apply for admission to the CSU International Programs in a Spanish-speaking country such as Chile, Mexico, or Spain for their junior or senior years or during graduate studies. Spanish skills must be sufficiently developed to permit satisfactory performance in a Spanish-language university. Please visit your counselor after transferring for additional information about these programs. For additional information, please visit: Department of World Languages &amp; Literatures .",
      "contentHtml": "<ol><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The B.A. in Spanish requires a \"C\" or higher in all courses applied to the major. </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Students interested in majoring in Spanish should demonstrate proficiency in the language through the second semester of intermediate level study prior to beginning upper-division courses.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Spanish is compatible with the B.A. in Spanish at Sacramento State. Students pursuing the Associate Degree for Transfer must complete all lower-division major coursework with a \"C\" or better.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Study Abroad: Students with an overall 2.75 GPA or higher are eligible to apply for admission to the CSU International Programs in a Spanish-speaking country such as Chile, Mexico, or Spain for their junior or senior years or during graduate studies. Spanish skills must be sufficiently developed to permit satisfactory performance in a Spanish-language university. Please visit your counselor after transferring for additional information about these programs. </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">For additional information, please visit: </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/college/arts-letters/world-languages-literatures/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Department of World Languages &amp; Literatures</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">.</span></li></ol>"
    }
  ],
